    "rulesTitle": "Rules (explained for beginners)",
    "rulesDescription": "Y is a two-player game. You can play locally against a friend or against one of our bots. Each turn, a player places a piece on an empty cell of the triangular board. The goal is to connect your pieces so they form a chain that touches the three edges of the board; the first player to do this wins the game.",
    "howToPlayTitle": "How to play — basic steps",
    "howToPlay": {
      "step1": "Players alternate turns; player A starts.",
      "step2": "On your turn, place a piece on any empty cell by clicking with the mouse.",
      "step3": "You cannot place a piece on a cell that is already occupied.",
      "step4": "If you are unsure which move to make, you can always use the suggestion button.",
      "step5": "After placing a piece, the turn passes to the other player or the bot.",
      "step6": "The game engine validates moves and automatically detects victory."
    },
    "boardSizeTitle": "Board size and strategy",
    "boardSizeDescription": "Board size changes the nature of the game: on small boards the game is mostly tactical (every move has a big impact), while on large boards the match becomes more strategic, with long-term planning and area control.",
    "tipsTitle": "Quick tips",
    "tip1": "Prioritize creating continuous connections instead of isolated pieces.",
    "tip2": "Block routes that allow your opponent to connect multiple sides.",
    "tip3": "Controlling the center early usually gives more connection options.",
    "finalParagraph": "Enjoy the game and try different board sizes to vary your strategy!"
  },
